      reinstall mints a NEW agent key, and force-reinstalling SOME peers in a namespace but not
      all lands them on different DNA hashes — different DHTs — a P2P partition (the alpha genesis
      PAIR must both get the flag). The validator LABELS the hash-moving class and stays silent on
      the coordinator-only one: the cheap path carries no trap, and an advisory on every
      coordinator edit would be the nag this registry exists to avoid. It never blocks. If the
      change can be expressed coordinator-side, do that; if it genuinely belongs in integrity,
      ride a planned lineage event with the whole namespace. Registry note: this rule is INLINE by
      design — `epr:validator-dna-hash-neutrality` is registered machinery with NO concern-canon
      row, because the ceremony tested DNA-hash-neutrality as a class and declined it ("no runtime
      predicate… it becomes the third registered validator, not a class").
